cff-version: 1.2.0
title: lpf-toolkit
abstract: >-
  A command-line driver and Jupyter notebooks for Ligand PathFinder, which
  builds Rosetta-based ligand and peptide (un)binding pathways. The upstream
  LigandPathFinder code is run unmodified.
message: >-
  If you use this toolkit, please cite the Ligand PathFinder method paper (in
  "references" below) — that is the work that deserves the citation. A mention
  of this toolkit is welcome but optional.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Arantes
    given-names: Pablo
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/pablo-arantes/lpf-toolkit"
keywords:
  - Rosetta
  - molecular modelling
  - ligand unbinding
  - protein-peptide
  - RosettaLigand
references:
